[[File:E 113.png|thumb|[[Heavenly Hippoe|Heavenly Hippoe]], the first example of an Angel enemy]]
'''Angel Enemies''' (Japanese: 天使 ''Tenshi'', '''Angels''') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]]. Like [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], Angels are often highly aggressive and tend to push with Area Attacks as well as high stats. They are nearly always mutually exclusive with the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] category of enemies. Design-wise, Angels are distinguished by the halo they all sport above their head.

See [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Angel abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Angel enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Angel enemies are associated with Yellow [[Catfruit]], which can be obtained from the [[Growing Catfruit]] stage [[Rays of Gold]].
*Anti-Angel abilities are improved by the [[Heaven's Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]].
*Angel [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Angel|Holy Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Angel|Holy Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Angel|Holy Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Holy Dawn]], [[Holy Apex]], [[Holy Refuge]]
**[[Divine Archangel Strikes]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*When first introduced to [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Angels were not targeted by "anti-all" units such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], encouraging use of dedicated [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel units]]. Though quickly changed, this was deliberate, as [[Angel Fanboy]]'s Japanese description used to say that special abilities other than anti-Angel abilities would not work ("Angels can't be hurt by non-Angelic attacks" in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]). Even after the "anti-all" units were updated to target Angels, Angel Fanboy's description remained the same until [[Version 6.6 Update|Version 6.6]], which added [[Youcan]], an Angel who can be affected by [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien abilities]].
*Many Angels' names end in "-el", which means "God" in Hebrew (ʾĒl) and is a common suffix in theological angels' names, such as [[wikipedia:Michael (archangel)|Michael]]. These include [[Gabriel]], [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], [[Mr. Angel]], [[Archangel Exiel]], [[Great Angel Chibinel]] and [[Tarsiriel]]; in [[BCJP]], there's also [[St. Dober]], due to "L" and "R" being homophones in Japanese, and [[Chickful A]], whose Japanese name is 天使ヒオコエル ''Tenshi Hiokoeru'' ("Angel Hiokoel").
**[[Heavenly Le'saint]]'s Japanese name, 大天使エルファント ''Daitenshi Erufanto'' ("Archangel Eruphant" or "Archangel Elphant"), combines エル ''Eru'' (El) with エレファント ''erefanto'' (elephant).
*The Angel trait is occasionally referred to as "Angelic", such as in [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Toaster]]'s description, [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Amber Egg: N110]]'s description and [[Mr. Angel]]'s pre-[[Version 13.3 Update|13.3]] [[Enemy Guide]] entry.
*Angel is the first enemy type whose Japanese name does not contain the word 敵 ''teki'' (enemy).
*[[Cala Maria]] and [[Heracrist (Enemy)|Heracrist]] are the only Angels to have single-target attacks.
*[[Bears Be Back]] are the only Angel enemy to have the Floating trait.
*[[Youcan]] and [[Bears Be Back]] are the only Angels to have any other traits.
*[[Serum (Enemy)|Serum]], [[Celesse (Enemy)|Celesse]], [[Fuu (Enemy)|Fuu]], [[Michelia (Enemy)|Michelia]] and [[Box Witch and Minions]] are the only non-Angel enemies to have halos.

